## 11. Documentation Output Location Policy (single authoritative docs tree)

- **One authoritative location.** Every AMSDP document, report, assessment, runbook, plan, manifest or evidence record an agent creates must be written under `/home/shomonrobie/amsdp/docs/`, in the subfolder that matches its subject: `audit/`, `architecture/`, `product/`, `governance/`, `implementation/`, `testing/`, `deployment/`, `security/`, `operations/`, plus the existing `demo/` and `decisions/`. Reuse an existing subfolder in preference to creating a new one; never create a near-duplicate folder (e.g. `docs/reports/` alongside `docs/audit/`).
- **`ai_factory/docs/` accepts no new AMSDP reports.** After the 2026-11-10 migration it holds only the agent-rules library (`agent-rules/`, path-bound by `workflows/engine.py` and `tests/unit/test_agent_rules.py` — never relocate it) and AI-Factory/AILI subsystem documentation. Do not write new AMSDP documents there, and do not treat it, `/tmp`, the repository root or any other directory as a fallback output location.
- **The AI Factory / AILI documents already in `ai_factory/docs/` stay there (owner decision O-1, 2026-11-10).** The 11 `AILI_*.md` reports and the AI-Factory reference documents (`architecture.md`, `operations.md`, `permissions.md`, `workflows.md`) document the AI Factory/AILI subsystem, not AMSDP product deliverables. Do not move, rename, delete or rewrite them, and do not add them to `docs/`. They are registered as intentionally out-of-tree in `docs/governance/AMSDP_Docs_Index_V1.0.md`. Reading them is normal and expected for AI Factory/AILI work; treating them as AMSDP report locations is not.
- **Never overwrite, never delete.** Check the destination filename before writing; if it already exists, stop and report the collision instead of overwriting. Historical versions are preserved — never delete, consolidate away or "clean up" an earlier version of a document.
- **Filenames** follow `AMSDP_<Topic>_<Version>.md` (or the exact existing name when a document is migrated). A rename is permitted only when it is recorded in the migration manifest.
- **Migrations are recorded acts.** Moving or renaming an existing document requires: destination collision check, byte-for-byte content preservation (SHA-256 before/after), and an entry in a manifest under `docs/governance/` giving original path, destination path, date and reason. Content must not be rewritten during a move. Files whose ownership or purpose is uncertain are not migrated — they are reported and left in place.
- **Owner-controlled documents are read-only.** They may be read and cited, but never modified, moved, renamed or overwritten without explicit Product Owner approval for that specific act: `docs/AMSDP_Master_Feature_List_V2.0_Draft.md`, `docs/AMSDP_Master_Feature_List_V2.1_Consolidated_Draft.md`, `docs/AMSDP_Master_Feature_List_V2.2_Consolidated_Draft.md`, `docs/AMSDP_Master_Feature_List_V2.3_Consolidated_Draft.md`; `docs/AMSDP_Business_Rules_V1.1.md` and `docs/product/AMSDP_Business_Rules_V1.0.md`; `docs/AMSDP_MVP_SCOPE_V1.1.md` and `docs/product/AMSDP_MVP_SCOPE_V1.0.md`; `docs/product/` product decisions and positioning; `docs/architecture/AMSDP_System_Architecture_V1.0.md`; `docs/AMSDP_Complete_ASCII_UI_UX_Blueprint.md`; the hackathon concept note; `docs/demo/AMSDP_Limitations_Report_V1.0.md` and `docs/demo/AMSDP_Demo_Credentials_V1.0.md`. The same principle extends to any other document the Product Owner subsequently declares authoritative.
- This section is additional to §1–§10. It relaxes none of them: §1 precedence, §3 non-negotiables, §6 compliance reporting, §7 evidence standard, §9 execution boundaries and the agent-rules library all continue to apply unchanged. Every report must state where it was written and, if it involved a migration, cite the manifest entry.

## 12. Documentation Reading & Retrieval Policy (consult `docs/` before acting)

- **Read before you plan, on your own initiative.** Every task begins by reading `docs/governance/AMSDP_Docs_Index_V1.0.md` — the single navigation index for the AMSDP document set. Use its *Read when* column to load the documents relevant to the identified domains. This is step 3 of §2. The project owner must never have to ask for it; if the index is missing or unreadable, say so and fall back to §4 routing plus a directory listing.
- **Locate documents by pattern, not by guess.** The AMSDP document set is `docs/` plus its subject subfolders (`audit/`, `architecture/`, `product/`, `governance/`, `implementation/`, `testing/`, `deployment/`, `security/`, `operations/`, `demo/`, `decisions/`). Filenames are `AMSDP_<Topic>_<Version>.md`. When the index and the tree disagree, the tree is the truth and the index is a defect to be fixed.
- **The index is a map, not the territory.** Cite the path you actually opened in this session. Never describe a document's contents you have not read, and never rely on remembered paths, remembered versions or remembered claims.
- **Read-only means read-and-cite, not never-read.** Product Owner-controlled documents (§11) must be read whenever relevant; only modification, movement or renaming is forbidden.
- **Source-of-truth order while reading:** verified runtime state → approved owner documents → AMSDP governance records → implementation/milestone reports → architectural intent. When two documents conflict, report the conflict; do not silently pick one (§1).
- **Context discipline (§9).** Read the index, then only the specific documents and sections needed. For very large documents (e.g. `docs/AMSDP_Complete_ASCII_UI_UX_Blueprint.md`, ~320 KB) use targeted search instead of loading the whole file, and never paste a large document into the conversation.
- **Secrets never travel.** `docs/demo/AMSDP_Demo_Credentials_V1.0.md` may be read to operate a demo, but no credential from it may be quoted into a report, log, commit message or reply (§3).
- **Keep the index current.** Creating, moving, renaming or retiring a document obligates an index update in the same task — plus a manifest entry for any move (§11). An unindexed document is an incomplete task.
- **Never ask the owner where to put a report or which document to read.** The folder follows §11 and the document follows §12. If a placement is genuinely ambiguous, choose the closest existing subfolder, state the rule you applied in the report, and raise it as an open item — do not block and do not ask in every prompt.

